## Proprietary Software Confidentiality and Restricted Access Agreement

Copyright (c) 2026 DJTS. All rights reserved.

This Proprietary Software Confidentiality and Restricted Access Agreement (this “Agreement”) is entered into by and between DJTS (the “Copyright Holder”) and any person or entity that accesses, views, uses, copies, downloads, or otherwise interacts with the Software (the “Recipient”).

For purposes of this Agreement, “Software” means all source code, object code, documentation, specifications, designs, interfaces, architecture, data, algorithms, trade secrets, and related materials made available by the Copyright Holder, whether in a private repository, by electronic transmission, or by any other restricted means, together with all copies, excerpts, backups, and derivative materials thereof.

By accessing or using the Software, Recipient agrees to be bound by this Agreement.

### 1. Ownership
All right, title, and interest in and to the Software, including all intellectual property rights therein, are and shall remain exclusively with the Copyright Holder. No right, title, or interest is transferred to Recipient except as expressly set forth in this Agreement.

### 2. Limited, Revocable Permission
Subject to strict compliance with this Agreement, the Copyright Holder grants Recipient a limited, personal, revocable, non-exclusive, non-transferable, and non-sublicensable permission to access and view the Software solely for the specific internal purpose expressly authorized in writing by the Copyright Holder. No other license or permission, express or implied, is granted.

### 3. Confidentiality Obligations
The Software is confidential, proprietary, and may constitute trade secret information. Recipient shall keep the Software in strict confidence and shall not disclose, publish, disseminate, or otherwise make available any portion of the Software to any third party without the prior written consent of the Copyright Holder.

### 4. Restrictions
Except to the extent expressly authorized in a separate written instrument signed by the Copyright Holder, Recipient shall not, and shall not permit any third party to:

a. copy, reproduce, download, clone, mirror, archive, scrape, or otherwise duplicate the Software;  
b. distribute, sell, resell, lease, lend, sublicense, assign, transfer, or otherwise convey the Software;  
c. modify, adapt, translate, port, localize, enhance, or create derivative works from the Software;  
d. reverse engineer, decompile, disassemble, decode, or otherwise attempt to derive the source code, structure, algorithms, or underlying ideas of the Software;  
e. remove, alter, obscure, or falsify any copyright, proprietary, or confidentiality notices;  
f. use the Software for benchmarking, competitive analysis, model training, fine-tuning, data extraction, or automated analysis;  
g. disclose screenshots, snippets, excerpts, issue contents, logs, or other non-public information derived from the Software;  
h. access or use the Software for any unlawful, unauthorized, or harmful purpose.

### 5. Access Security
Recipient shall not share credentials, tokens, invitations, or other access mechanisms used to obtain access to the Software. Any access granted is personal to Recipient and may be revoked at any time, with or without cause, in the sole discretion of the Copyright Holder.

### 6. Return and Destruction
Upon the Copyright Holder’s request, or upon termination of Recipient’s access for any reason, Recipient shall immediately cease all use of the Software and shall permanently delete or destroy all copies, excerpts, backups, notes, and derivative materials in Recipient’s possession or control, except to the extent retention is required by applicable law.

### 7. Termination
Any breach of this Agreement shall result in automatic termination of all permissions granted hereunder, without notice or further action by the Copyright Holder. Upon termination, Recipient shall remain bound by the confidentiality and destruction obligations set forth herein.

### 8. No Warranty
THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED “AS IS” AND “AS AVAILABLE,” WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, WHETHER EXPRESS, IMPLIED, STATUTORY, OR OTHERWISE, INCLUDING WITHOUT LIMITATION WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, TITLE, AND NON-INFRINGEMENT.

### 9. Limitation of Liability
TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, THE COPYRIGHT HOLDER SHALL NOT BE LIABLE FOR ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL, EXEMPLARY, OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES, OR FOR ANY LOSS OF PROFITS, REVENUE, DATA, BUSINESS, OR GOODWILL, ARISING OUT OF OR RELATING TO THE SOFTWARE OR THIS AGREEMENT, WHETHER IN CONTRACT, TORT, OR OTHERWISE, EVEN IF ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGES.

### 10. Equitable Relief
Recipient acknowledges that any breach of this Agreement may cause irreparable harm for which monetary damages may be inadequate. The Copyright Holder shall be entitled to seek injunctive relief, specific performance, and any other equitable or legal remedy available at law or in equity, without the necessity of posting bond or proving actual damages, to the extent permitted by law.

### 11. No Waiver
No failure or delay by the Copyright Holder in exercising any right, power, or remedy under this Agreement shall operate as a waiver thereof, nor shall any single or partial exercise preclude any other or further exercise of any right, power, or remedy.

### 12. Governing Law and Jurisdiction
This Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of India, without regard to conflict-of-law principles. Any dispute, controversy, or claim arising out of or relating to this Agreement, including its formation or breach, shall be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the competent courts located in Ahmedabad, Gujarat, India.

### 13. Severability
If any provision of this Agreement is held to be invalid or unenforceable, the remaining provisions shall remain in full force and effect to the maximum extent permitted by law.

### 14. Entire Agreement
This Agreement constitutes the entire agreement between the parties with respect to the Software and supersedes all prior or contemporaneous understandings, whether oral or written. Any amendment or waiver must be in a writing signed by the Copyright Holder.

